          "explanation": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><p>$\\bar{x} = (91.6 + 88.75 + 90.8 + 89.95 + 91.3)/5 = 452.40/5 = 90.48$. Since $\\sigma$ is KNOWN, use the $z$-interval: margin $= z_{0.025}\\,\\sigma/\\sqrt{n} = 1.960 \\times 3/\\sqrt{5} = 1.960 \\times 1.34164 = 2.6296$. So the interval is $90.48 \\pm 2.63 = (87.85,\\ 93.11)$.</p></div><div class=\"ml-vi\"><p>$\\bar{x} = (91.6 + 88.75 + 90.8 + 89.95 + 91.3)/5 = 452.40/5 = 90.48$. Vì $\\sigma$ ĐÃ BIẾT nên dùng khoảng tin cậy theo $z$: sai số $= z_{0.025}\\,\\sigma/\\sqrt{n} = 1.960 \\times 3/\\sqrt{5} = 1.960 \\times 1.34164 = 2.6296$. Vậy khoảng là $90.48 \\pm 2.63 = (87.85,\\ 93.11)$.</p></div>"
